# Line endings are LF everywhere, in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# Without this, git on Windows checks files out with CRLF while the build
# writes LF, so every generated page compares as changed. In the public
# repository that meant a fresh clone failed `node tools/check.js` with
# thirty-one stale-page errors - which is the first thing CONTRIBUTING.md asks
# a contributor to run, so the project appeared broken before they had touched
# anything.
#
# It is also why check.js could never have caught a real staleness problem on
# Windows: everything was always stale.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries must not be touched at all. A woff2 or a png with its bytes
# rewritten is a corrupt file, not a tidied one.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.zip binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.mp4 binary
*.mp3 binary
*.wav binary
*.pdf binary
